        "id": "mq-deepdives-overview",
        "title": "Technology Deep Dives Overview",
        "content": "These are the four message queue systems you will encounter most often in production. Together they cover the main categories: traditional broker, distributed log, cloud-managed, and lightweight/embedded. Each section explains how the system works at a low level, provides a runnable code example, and lists where it shines and where it falls short.\n\n---"
